[*
Purpose:
UTC time helpers built in Raden itself over the Os module.

Design notes:
- All conversions take a non-negative epoch-seconds integer. Taking the epoch
  as an argument keeps every conversion deterministic and easy to test; the
  zero-arg forms simply feed them Time::now.
- Times are UTC only. Negative epochs are rejected because the VM's % and //
  truncate toward zero.
- Durations use Os::clock (monotonic milliseconds), never wall time, so they
  are safe across wall-clock changes.

Exports:
- hh-of / mm-of / ss-of : epoch -> hour / minute / second
- hms-of                : epoch -> "HH:MM:SS"
- ymd-of                : epoch -> "YYYY-MM-DD"
- iso-of                : epoch -> "YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ"
- now                   : -> current epoch seconds
- hms / ymd / iso       : zero-arg conveniences over now
- clock-ms              : -> monotonic milliseconds since an arbitrary point
- sleep-ms              : milliseconds -> true after sleeping
- elapsed-ms            : start-clock-ms -> milliseconds elapsed since start

Examples:
"Time" load

0 Time::hms-of print                   -- prints 00:00:00
951868800 Time::ymd-of print           -- prints 2000-03-01
Time::now Time::iso-of print           -- prints 2026-08-22T12:34:56Z

Time::clock-ms start let
50 Time::sleep-ms pop
start Time::elapsed-ms print           -- prints >= 50

*]

"Typecheck" load
"Core" load
"Os" load

Typecheck::OGTypes open
Core::@str open

Time module

    [* ---- private helpers ---- *]

    __pad2 (Int) (Str) defun
        n let
        n 10 < if
            [* to_string keeps the original, so drain it: the Core::@str idiom *]
            "0" n @str append
        else
            n @str
        end
    end

    __pad4 (Int) (Str) defun
        n let
        n 100 < if
            "00" n @str append
        else
            n 1000 < if
                "0" n @str append
            else
                n @str
            end
        end
    end

    __check-epoch (Int) () defun
        epoch let
        epoch 0 < if
            "time: epoch must be non-negative" error
        end
    end

    [* ---- epoch-taking core ---- *]

    hh-of (Int) (Int) defun
        dup Time::__check-epoch call
        86400 %
        3600 //
    end

    mm-of (Int) (Int) defun
        dup Time::__check-epoch call
        86400 %
        3600 %
        60 //
    end

    ss-of (Int) (Int) defun
        dup Time::__check-epoch call
        60 %
    end

    hms-of (Int) (Str) defun
        dup Time::__check-epoch call
        epoch let

        [* build functionally: string variables must not be held across a
           nested call boundary because scope materialization resolves them *]

        epoch Time::hh-of call Time::__pad2 call
        ":"
        epoch Time::mm-of call Time::__pad2 call
        ":"
        epoch Time::ss-of call Time::__pad2 call
        append append append append
    end

    ymd-of (Int) (Str) defun
        dup Time::__check-epoch call
        epoch let

        [* civil-from-days: Howard Hinnant's algorithm, valid for epoch >= 0 *]

        epoch 86400 // days let
        days 719468 + z let
        z 146097 // era let
        z era 146097 * - doe let
        doe doe 1460 // - doe 36524 // + doe 146096 // - 365 // yoe let
        yoe era 400 * + year let
        doe yoe 365 * yoe 4 // + yoe 100 // - - doy let
        doy 5 * 2 + 153 // mp let
        mp 10 < if
            mp 3 +
        else
            mp 9 -
        end
        month let
        month 2 <= if
            year 1 + year set
        end
        doy 153 mp * 2 + 5 // - 1 + day let

        year Time::__pad4 call
        "-"
        month Time::__pad2 call
        "-"
        day Time::__pad2 call
        append append append append
    end

    iso-of (Int) (Str) defun
        dup Time::__check-epoch call
        epoch let

        epoch Time::ymd-of call
        "T"
        epoch Time::hms-of call
        "Z"
        append append append
    end

    [* ---- zero-arg conveniences over now ---- *]

    now () (Int) defun
        Os::now call
    end

    hms () (Str) defun
        Time::now call Time::hms-of call
    end

    ymd () (Str) defun
        Time::now call Time::ymd-of call
    end

    iso () (Str) defun
        Time::now call Time::iso-of call
    end

    [* ---- durations (monotonic clock) ---- *]

    clock-ms () (Int) defun
        Os::clock call
    end

    sleep-ms (Int) (Bool) defun
        Os::sleep call
    end

    elapsed-ms (Int) (Int) defun
        start let
        Time::clock-ms call start -
    end

    [* ---- aliases ---- *]

    @hh-of apply Time::hh-of call end
    @mm-of apply Time::mm-of call end
    @ss-of apply Time::ss-of call end
    @hms-of apply Time::hms-of call end
    @ymd-of apply Time::ymd-of call end
    @iso-of apply Time::iso-of call end
    @now apply Time::now call end
    @hms apply Time::hms call end
    @ymd apply Time::ymd call end
    @iso apply Time::iso call end
    @clock-ms apply Time::clock-ms call end
    @sleep-ms apply Time::sleep-ms call end
    @elapsed-ms apply Time::elapsed-ms call end

end
